    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d390">

                <pb facs="0469" n="459" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg459"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5151/934: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-21T15:00:00+07:00">June 21, 1943—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 21—2:02 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>988. From Adler to Secretary of Treasury only. TF–133. Dr. Kung sent for me on
                    Saturday and asked if there had been any reply to the question submitted to you
                    in TF–128.<anchor n="83" xml:id="d390-f1"/> When I answered in the negative, he
                    said he would appreciate receiving Treasury’s response fairly soon, as unless
                    some action is taken the Agreement would expire at the end of the month.
                    [Adler.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
